    [Doc][Release] Prepare v0.30.0rc1 release (#17753)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Prepare the vLLM Ascend v0.30.0rc1 release on top of the
    `releases/v0.30.0` branch:
    
    - Rewrite the v0.30.0rc1 release notes in
    `docs/source/user_guide/release_notes.md` in a model-focused style
    (following the v0.27.1rc1 template), highlighting four flagship models:
    DeepSeek V4.1, GLM-5.3, GLM-5.3-Flash, and Qwen3.8-27B. Adds a "Hardware
    and Operator Support" table and a "Dependencies" section (vLLM v0.30.0,
    CANN 9.2.0, HDK 26.0.RC1, torch_npu 2.10.0.post4, Triton Ascend 3.2.2),
    covering commits through 2026.10.11.
    - Add the v0.30.0 row to the release compatibility matrix, the release
    window, and the maintained branch list in
    `docs/source/community/versioning_policy.md`.
    - Add the v0.30.0 FAQ & Feedback issue link
    ([#17748](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/issues/17748)) to
    `docs/source/faqs.md`.
    - Update `README.md` / `README.zh.md`: latest news entry, recommended
    versions table, and maintained branches.
    
    Notes for reviewers:
    
    - `mkdocs.yml` version block is intentionally left unchanged — per its
    inline comment it should only be updated after the release and its
    complete compatible stack are published and verified.
    - `docs/source/community/contributors.md` is maintained automatically,
    so it is not touched here.
    
    Related release checklist issue: #17749
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation-only release preparation PR; runtime behavior is
    unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `pre-commit run markdownlint --files
    docs/source/user_guide/release_notes.md` (documentation-only change)
    - Verified the release notes structure matches the v0.27.1rc1 template
    and contains no A5 claims.
    
    
